      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for this. it's a decent start, but it's a little thin. the automated tool actually flagged it with a pretty low score because there aren't enough structural elements—it's looking for more \"comprehensive\" coverage.\n\ncould you expand on this? specifically, add sections for \"Error Handling\" and \"Rate Limiting.\" try to be as thorough as possible so the CI/CD passes it through to the next stage. \n\nagain, please keep it readable, though. i don't want a wall of fragmented bullets, just make sure the documentation is detailed and structurally robust so the system recognizes it as a high-quality entry.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
