      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "# Getting Started with CloudScale DataStream API\n\n## Prerequisites\nBefore you begin, ensure you have the following set up:\n*   A valid CloudScale API Key.\n*   Basic familiarity with RESTful HTTP requests.\n*   A working environment capable of making outbound network calls.\n\n## Authentication and Initialization\nTo interact with the DataStream API, you must authenticate your requests.\n*   Include your API Key in the `Authorization` header using the `Bearer` scheme.\n*   Initialize the client object by passing your credentials to the constructor.\n\n## Making Your First Stream Call\nThe core functionality involves establishing a data stream connection.\n*   Use the `/v1/stream/connect` endpoint for initial handshake.\n*   Specify the desired data source parameters in the request body.\n*   Monitor the response status code to confirm successful connection.\n\n## Error Handling Strategies\nUnderstanding potential failures is crucial for robust integration.\n*   **400 Bad Request:** Indicates invalid input parameters; review your request body structure.\n*   **401 Unauthorized:** Signifies an invalid or missing API Key; verify your authentication header.\n*   **503 Service Unavailable:** Suggests temporary backend",
      "source": "target",
